// V4 mistakes are conflicts between facts the book can otherwise explain.
// Run `axiom check examples/03-violations.ax` to see each one at its source.

base USD
use std
use us/401k
use us/529

entity me : person
  born 1988-04-12
  filing single
  lives us

entity acme : employer
entity fidelity
entity chase
entity trader-joes : grocer
entity theater

account checking : deposit at chase
account education-fund : deposit at chase
account retirement : 401k at fidelity
account brokerage : brokerage at fidelity
account wallet : asset
  holds BTC

commodity BTC : crypto
  precision 8
commodity VTI : fund
  precision 3

entity scholarship : grant
  purpose education
  until 2026-12-31

// A misspelled property is refused at the declaration.
account college : 529-plan at fidelity
  benificiary me
// expect: unknown property `benificiary`, with `beneficiary` suggested.

opening 2025-12-31
  checking 100_000 USD

// The 2026 deferral limit is 24,500 USD; the owner is under 50.
2026-01-30 retirement <- acme 26_000 USD
// expect: `deferral-limit`, 1,500 USD over the annual cap.

// All pre-tax value in the account has no basis; this $10,000 withdrawal is
// taxable and carries the early-withdrawal penalty for an owner aged 37.
2026-02-02 retirement -> checking 10_000 USD
// expect: 1,000 USD of early-withdrawal tax, owed with the return.

// With no lot policy, a quarter of a coin could come from either purchase.
2026-02-10 checking        -> wallet   0.5 BTC @ 60_000 USD
2026-02-20 checking        -> wallet   0.5 BTC @ 90_000 USD
2026-03-01 wallet 0.25 BTC -> checking         @ 96000.00 USD
// expect: ambiguous relief. The two candidate gains are 9,000 USD and 1,500 USD.

// Trader Joe's says groceries; the explicit purpose disagrees.
2026-03-02 checking -> trader-joes 84.20 USD #rent
// expect: a purpose conflict: the grocer says groceries, the flow says rent.

// Four shares at this price cost 1,142.80 USD, not 1,000 USD.
2026-03-04 checking 1_000 USD -> brokerage 4 VTI @ 285.70 USD
// expect: a price mismatch of 142.80 USD (4 shares cost 1,142.80 USD).

// The scholarship's money stays in its own account, so the theater payment
// cannot use unrestricted checking parcels instead.
2026-04-01 education-fund <- scholarship 1_200 USD
2026-04-02 education-fund -> theater     300 USD   #fun
// expect: `purpose`, since scholarship money is restricted to education.

// The scholarship account keeps the remaining grant money identifiable through
// the deadline. The bank balance assertions show both positions at year end.
2026-12-31 checking       = 57_915.80 USD
2026-12-31 education-fund = 900 USD
// expect: `deadline`, with 900 USD of education money still unspent.
